{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541419-alternative-arcanum-attainments","id":1541419,"title":"Alternative Arcanum attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-02T17:19:04-07:00","id":1541419,"title":"Alternative Arcanum attainments","content":"Some arcana attainments like Fate 2's conditional duration are so impactful to the use of the arcana that I can't imagine not taking them, but others definitely feel more niche. I made the ones below to better fit the types of campaigns I was in, but wanted to hear if people had come up with interesting alternatives to the norm.<br /> <br /> Death 2, Long shadow - You can affect a target as if in touch range so long as your shadows are touching. Spend a mana to project your shadow out to use sensory range instead of reach.<br /> <br /> Forces 2, - Your control of your own body becomes supernaturally precise. You can add half your forces dots to any physical skill check, even if untrained. (Athletics, Brawl etc.)<br /> <br /> Mind 2, Consideration - Your peripheral mage sight pings when the attention of others is on you. When you spend a mana to keep mage sight active for a scene you can get a sense of whose attention it is and even a sense of their intentions.<br /> <br /> Mind 4, Astral Projection - As you would meditate into the astral, you can project yourself as a goetia into the mundane world. In this form you lose your body's senses and navigate the world under mind-sight, unless you activate the mage sight of other arcanum. You lose a mana per scene in this form, and when you have none, are forcibly snapped back to your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","user":"Hydrophiliak","date":". 09-02-2024, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T09:53:08-07:00","id":1541457,"title":"","content":"I'm a little iffy on the others, but I find the last to be both a drastic departure from the usual boundaries of Attainments and just a thing that can already be done as a spell at that Arcanum level, but worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:18:32-07:00","id":1541468,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second Isator here. While I could see these concepts working for Legacy Attainments in the right context (even so, maybe with some refinement) the Death one is the only one that actually feels like an Arcanum Attainment in design function. <br /> <br /> Though even then I'm not sure if the Death 2 one is just a lesser version of Space but cheaper for being far more niche in application, or kinda ridiculous with whatever &quot;projecting your shadow&quot; means (considering how Space and Time require 1 reach, a special Yantra, and 1 mana to cast at stuff they can't see, 1 mana to overcome the normal range rules needs some serious caveats). It feels like it would be easier to modify the Aimed Spell rules with your shadow as the manifestation of the ranged attack, and some sort of bonus against those unsuspecting that your shadow can carry magic with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T14:55:59-07:00","id":1541485,"title":"","content":"If you're going to replace Mind 2 with anything (and I don't necessarily think you should), it should just be Astral Adept. It's a somewhat overpriced merit with a specific niche that falls under Mind's purview","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T08:03:01-07:00","id":1541531,"title":"","content":"I think Astral Adept is a finely priced Merit relative to the fact that the normal avenues for travel to the Astral Realms are a big part of the flavour of the whole experience and the means to disregard them should be fairly limited.<br /> <br /> An Attainment for a shallow dive into an Arcanum to do so would be quite objectionable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T17:49:43-07:00","id":1541551,"title":"","content":"I think the second Attainments of Death, Mind and Spirit are pretty useful. Not only do they save a spell slot from an Unveiling spell to see the subject of their purview, but they save you a second spell slot by allowing the mage to interact with them by paying mana. They offer solid and fundamental utility.<br /> <br /> The one I would change is that of Mind 4, <i>Intuitive Leap</i>. An alternative Attainment would be to change primary factors by paying a point of mana, as the mage shifts their attention on the Imago between sustained (Duration) and selective (Potency).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-04-2024, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}